```

`hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow` is added to the `PayInvoiceArgs` type, but the `payInvoice` function (line ~11401) never destructures this field and never passes it to `getPayMoneyRequestParams`. This means the type field is dead code. Additionally, `getPayMoneyRequestParams` calls `buildPolicyData` (line ~9405) without passing `hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow`, so the invoice-payment code path that creates a workspace will still produce duplicate onboarding tasks -- the same bug this PR aims to fix.

Either remove `hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow` from `PayInvoiceArgs` if the invoice path is not affected, or complete the propagation:
1. Destructure `hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow` in `payInvoice`
2. Add it to the `getPayMoneyRequestParams` parameter type
3. Pass it through to the `buildPolicyData` call at line ~9405

```ts
// In payInvoice (line ~11401):
function payInvoice({
    // ... existing params ...
    hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow,
}: PayInvoiceArgs) {
    // ...
    } = getPayMoneyRequestParams({
        // ... existing params ...
        hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow,
    });

// In getPayMoneyRequestParams, pass to buildPolicyData:
    } = buildPolicyData({
        // ... existing params ...
        hasCompletedGuidedSetupFlow,
    });
```

