The `tabRef` property is defined in `ScrollToTabProps` (in `types.ts`) but is no longer used by the new unified `scrollToTab` implementation. Previously, the web-only implementation used `tabRef` for `scrollIntoView`, and the native implementation ignored it. Now that both platforms use the same implementation based on `containerRef.current.scrollTo()`, `tabRef` is never read anywhere in `scrollToTab`.

All callers in `TabSelectorContext.tsx` still pass `tabRef`, making it dead code throughout the call chain.

Remove `tabRef` from `ScrollToTabProps` in `types.ts` and stop passing it from callers in `TabSelectorContext.tsx`:

```typescript
// types.ts - remove tabRef
type ScrollToTabProps = {
    animated?: boolean;
    containerRef: React.RefObject<RNScrollView | null>;
    containerX: number;
    containerWidth: number;
    tabX: number;
    tabWidth: number;
};
```

