The `aria-selected` prop is redundant. React Native automatically maps `accessibilityState.selected` to the `aria-selected` attribute on web platforms. Adding both creates unnecessary duplication.

**Suggested fix:**
Remove the `aria-selected` prop and keep only `accessibilityState`:
```tsx
<PressableWithFeedback
    onPress={onPress}
    role={CONST.ROLE.TAB}
    accessibilityLabel={`${translate('initialSettingsPage.account')}, ${translate('sidebarScreen.buttonMySettings')}`}
    wrapperStyle={styles.flex1}
    accessibilityState={{selected: isSelected}}
    style={({hovered}) => [style, hovered && styles.navigationTabBarItemHovered]}
    sentryLabel={CONST.SENTRY_LABEL.NAVIGATION_TAB_BAR.ACCOUNT}
>
```

